#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
SlowOS E-ink Bridge Daemon
Captures the Xorg root (Phase 2: panel-first 960×680 on :0) and pushes to Waveshare 13.3" e-Paper (K).

Phase 2.5 env (default ON via SLOWOS_EINK_PHASE25=1; set 0 to disable QoL paths):
  SLOWOS_EINK_POINTER_HZ — pointer-led partial attempt rate cap (default 6); not starved by MD5 coalesce.
  SLOWOS_EINK_RECONCILE_SEC — min interval for anti-stale displayed-model vs capture audit (default 3).
  SLOWOS_EINK_ESCAL_SOFT_SEC — from first push failure, force full-panel partial by this deadline (default 3).
  SLOWOS_EINK_ESCAL_HARD_SEC — from first push failure, force full mono refresh path by this deadline (default 6).
  SLOWOS_EINK_REGION_CAP — dual-track max regions per partial frame, 2–4 (default 3); pointer wins on overflow.
  SLOWOS_EINK_POINTER_ARENA — half-size-ish bbox padding px around cursor for pointer track (default 96).
  SLOWOS_EINK_RESTART_GRACE_SEC — after hard escal deadline, consecutive failures before exec restart (default 2).
  SLOWOS_EINK_WATCHDOG_FRAMES — after this many captures with no push, byte-compare _last_push_l vs frame; if
    different, force a push (breaks MD5 / stale-belief deadlocks). Default 24 (~4s at 6 Hz).
  SLOWOS_EINK_FOCUS_HINTS — use xdotool active-window geometry as an extra dirty hint (default 1).
  SLOWOS_EINK_FOCUS_POLL_HZ — how often to poll active window id/geometry (default 4).
  SLOWOS_EINK_POINTER_TRAIL — union previous and current pointer arenas to reduce ghost cursors (default 1).
  SLOWOS_EINK_FOCUS_RESYNC_SEC — bounded partial over focused window (default 0 off). If >0, only runs
    when tile hotpath shows dirty pixels (``last_dirty_area_px_raw`` > 0), not on hash-quiet geometry-only.
  SLOWOS_EINK_PERIODIC_FULL_MONO — when 1, push-count ladder can force full mono every ``SLOWOS_EINK_FULL_REFRESH_EVERY``
    successful pushes (legacy). Default 0: full mono only from ``_force_full_refresh_next`` (degraded / T+6 / hygiene).
  SLOWOS_EINK_FOCUS_RESYNC_MIN_CAPTURES — min captures-without-push before a resync may fire (default 6).
  SLOWOS_EINK_TYPING_PRIORITY_STREAK — when focus is active and hash_same_count reaches this, suppress
    pointer-led pushes so content/hash paths are not starved (default 6).
  SLOWOS_XWD_NATIVE — when 1 (default), use /usr/local/bin/slowos-xwd-to-gray for fast BGRX→L if present.
  SLOWOS_XWD_TO_GRAY — override path to the native XWD→gray helper (default /usr/local/bin/slowos-xwd-to-gray).
  SLOWOS_EINK_ANTIROLLBACK_HASH_FULLRECT — after each successful hash-led partial (not already full-rect),
    force one full-panel partial on the next push to anchor pigment to latest GUI (default 1).
  SLOWOS_EINK_TEXT_FRESHNESS — when 1 (default), focus-aware typing/search: bypass min_push_interval for
    hash pushes and drain a short FIFO of distinct intermediate captures so bursts are not skipped.
  SLOWOS_EINK_TEXT_CAPTURE_FIFO — retain up to 12 overwritten distinct-hash frames for FIFO drain (default 1).
  SLOWOS_EINK_CURSOR_BLEACH_PARTIALS — before each partial in cursor_pin overlap, one SPI pass with white-filled
    pin hull in the 1-bit buffer, then the real frame partial (default 1).
  SLOWOS_EINK_WATCHDOG_INK_DOUBT_FRAMES — after this many captures-without-push, force watchdog even if
    belief bytes match capture (default 2× SLOWOS_EINK_WATCHDOG_FRAMES).
  SLOWOS_EINK_PASS_PTR_P95_MS / SLOWOS_EINK_PASS_PTR_HZ_5S / SLOWOS_EINK_PASS_TYPE_P95_MS — PASS/FAIL gates for
    ``pointer_responsiveness_judgment`` / ``typing_freshness_judgment`` in status (defaults conservative for e-ink).
  SLOWOS_EINK_OPERATOR_EVENT_PATH — default ``/run/eink-bridge.operator_event``: line ``flicker`` when you see
    rollback on glass; or JSON ``{"cursor_test":{"loops":N,"residue_score":S,"pass":bool}}`` (flat keys also ok).
    ``kill -USR1`` to the bridge PID records the same flicker mark.

  Dual-track overlap (Phase 2.6): content dirty rects that touch the pointer arena are merged into that
  arena (union) so they are never dropped; see ``_dual_track_regions``.

  Phase 2.5 producer/consumer (when ``SLOWOS_EINK_PHASE25``): producer captures at ``--fps`` into the
  latest-frame slot and a short distinct-hash FIFO for typing bursts; consumer owns diff, scheduling,
  SPI, and ``_last_push_l`` (scheduling aid only; see contract below).

DISPLAYED-MODEL CACHE CONTRACT (SSD16xx / epd13in3k partial path):

- ``_last_push_l`` is a **scheduling aid** (diff + partial tiling), not proof that physical pigment
  matches the latest GUI capture; never treat byte equality with capture as “the panel is correct.”
- Every diff compares ``_last_push_l`` → latest captured ``frame`` (truth from X root + overlay).
- After a partial that updates only rectangles R_i, belief is patched with ``paste`` from ``frame``
  only over ⋃ R_i — never overwrite full belief after a successful sub-panel partial.
- ``_last_pushed_hash`` is the MD5 hex of ``_last_push_l`` (belief digest). It must not be set to
  ``md5(frame)`` after a partial-only success, or the scheduler falsely treats software as synced while
  unstirred pixels still differ from capture (stale-frame / rollback-like flicker).
- On any exception or logical push failure paths: **never** mutate ``_last_push_l`` / ``partial_count``
  escalation state as if the ink updated; bump ``cache_confidence`` toward ``degraded`` and escalate
  the next refresh (minimum full-panel partial waveform; full monochrome refresh periodically).

Architecture:
  Production: SlowOS on :0 at panel resolution → xwd root → SPI e-ink (1:1 when WxH matches).
  Optional: Xvfb (:99) at 960×680 only if started without --no-xvfb (not Phase 2 default).

Usage:
  ./eink-bridge.py              # Run with defaults
  ./eink-bridge.py --display :0 # Use existing X display instead of Xvfb
  ./eink-bridge.py --fps 2      # Poll at 2 Hz (default: 6 Hz; override SLOWOS_EINK_FPS or --fps)
"""

